## Tooling: `drover`

[`drover`](https://github.com/ravinald/drover) drives the work in this project:
the backlog, the completion ledger, result capture, and the prompt an agent is
handed. It finds the project by walking up to `.drover.toml`, so it runs from
anywhere inside the tree.

A work item is one file at `{{ .Bodies }}/<NN>-<slug>.md`: metadata in a leading
`---` fence, prose below. The directory listing is the backlog, so adding an item
needs no config edit and no change to drover.

The fence is driver metadata, not part of what a run is asked to do. The prompt
is everything under it, and its numbered requirements are the contract.
{{ if .Namespaces }}
Ids without a prefix are the planned backlog. Prefixed ids arrive from the
tracker:
{{ range .Namespaces }}
- `{{ .Prefix }}` — {{ .Kind }}
{{- end }}
{{ end }}
Frontmatter is a closed schema. An undeclared key is a parse error, because a
typo'd `deps` would read as no dependencies and render a blocked item READY.

- Required (may be empty, may not be absent): {{ range $i, $k := .Required }}{{ if $i }}, {{ end }}`{{ $k }}`{{ end }}
{{- if .Optional }}
- Optional: {{ range $i, $k := .Optional }}{{ if $i }}, {{ end }}`{{ $k }}`{{ end }}
{{- end }}
{{- if .Closes }}
- `closes` holds the tracker issue numbers this item resolves. `drover resolve
  <id> <n> <disposition>` records a judgment on one and refuses a number the key
  does not name; `--link` adds it to the key first. `drover finish` closes each
  issue recorded `fixed`, and `drover check` reports `NO DISPOSITION` for a
  merged item whose key names an issue nobody judged. An item that leaves the key
  empty closes nothing when it merges.
{{- end }}
{{- if .Issue }}
- `issue` is the tracker issue `drover intake` created this item from. `finish`
  reads `closes`, not `issue`, so an item meant to close its own intake issue
  names it in both.
{{- if .SeedCloses }}
  This project sets `[intake] closes = "issue"`, so intake writes the number
  into both; remove it from `closes` when the item is a split or only partly
  fixes the issue.
{{- else if .Closes }}
  `[intake] closes = "issue"` makes intake write it into both.
{{- end }}
{{- end }}

